---
/*
  The results band.

  These numbers are the single most persuasive thing on a case study page and
  they used to sit inside the reading column at the same width as a paragraph.
  Now the band breaks the page, goes to ink, and gives them the size they earn.

  Still a plain grid: a study with one number gets one column, not three columns
  with two holes in them.
*/
---

<div data-tone="dark" class="relative left-1/2 my-20 w-screen -translate-x-1/2 bg-surface py-16 md:py-20" data-stats>
  <div class="container-bleed">
    <div class="grid gap-12 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-10">
      <slot />
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
